---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const faqs = [
  ['Do I need an account?', 'No account is required for personal tracking or local splits. Optional usernames for sharing with other Money Plant users are planned, not available in the current release.'],
  ['Does it work without internet?', 'Expenses, budgets, local splits and reports work offline. Update checks contact GitHub. Opening payment links or sharing a file may use another app and a connection. Future username sharing will sync selected splits when connected.'],
  ['Where is my data stored?', 'Records stay in the app’s private storage on your device. A local SQLite storage upgrade is in development and is not yet in the published APK. Storage is not encrypted; device authentication adds an app access lock.'],
  ['How do backup and restore work?', 'Export a backup from Settings and keep your own copy. Restore from that file when needed. Exported files contain personal financial data. Future username identity and device transfer will have a separate recovery process.'],
  ['How do I install or update?', 'Download the Android APK from a release shown here and follow the install guide. Back up first. A matching app identity and signing key let Android install an update over the existing app. Do not uninstall to troubleshoot without preserving your backup.'],
  ['Is there an iPhone version?', 'Android is the only published download at present. Other platforms are ideas on the roadmap, with no release date.'],
];
---
<section class="container-site faq-section">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</p><h2>Curious minds ask.</h2></div>
  {faqs.map(([q,a]) => <details class="faq-item" name="faq"><summary>{q}<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
  <p>Need a hand? <a class="text-link" href={`${base}/install`}>Read the install guide</a> or <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/devmer2311/MoneyPlant/issues">ask on GitHub</a>.</p>
  <p><a class="text-link" href="#backup-guide">Watch the backup & restore walkthrough ↑</a></p>
</section>
